          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Baer sum
            is the natural addition operation on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group+extensions"} abelian group extensions
            as well on the extensions of
            = succeed "-modules," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            are classified by the degree-2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi Grp
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^2_{Grp}(G,A) = H^2(\mathbf{B}G, A) = H(\mathbf{B}G, \mathbf{B}^2 A)
                  \\,.
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycles"} cocycles
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G \to \mathbf{B}^2 A
            there is a canonical addition operation coming from the additive structure of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p Below are discussed several different equivalent ways to define the Baer sum
          %h3#on_concrete_cocycles On concrete cocycles
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            in degree-2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi Grp
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^2_{Grp}(G,A)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  c : G \times G \to A
          %p satisfying the cocycle property.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Given two cocycles
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 2
                    %mo :
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_1, c_2 : G \times G \to A
              their
              %strong sum
              is the composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Δ
                          %mrow
                            %mi G
                            %mo ×
                            %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi c
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi c
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (c_1 + c_2) : G \times G \stackrel{\Delta_{G \times G}}{\to} (G \times G) \times (G \times G) \stackrel{(c_1,c_2)}{\to} A \times A \stackrel{+}{\to} A
            %p of
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal"} diagonal
                  on
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                          %mo ×
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G\times G
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+product"} direct product
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi c
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi c
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c_1,c_2)
              %li
                %p
                  the group operation
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mi A
                          %mo ×
                          %mi A
                          %mo →
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} + \colon A \times A \to A
            %p
              Hence for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_1, g_2 \in G
              this sum is the function that sends
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (c_1 + c_2) : (g_1, g_2) \mapsto c_1(g_1,g_2) + c_2(g_1, g_2)
          %h3#on_abstract_cocycles On abstract cocycles
          %p
            As discussed at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi G
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \colon G \times G \to A
            is equivalently a morphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoids"} 2-groupoids
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            to the double-delooping
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid"} 2-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^2 A
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 2
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  c_1,c_2 : \mathbf{B}G \to \mathbf{B}^2 A
                  \\,.
          %p
            Since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is an abelian group,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^2 A
            is naturally an abelian
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-group"} 3-group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 2
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 2
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} + \colon (\mathbf{B}^2 A) \times (\mathbf{B}^A)\to \mathbf{B}^2 A
          %p With respect to this the sum operation is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 2
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ×
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  c_1 + c_2 : \mathbf{B}G \stackrel{\Delta_{\mathbf{B}G}}{\to} \mathbf{B}G \times   \mathbf{B}G \stackrel{(c_1,c_2)}{\to} \mathbf{B}^2 A \times \mathbf{B}^2 A \stackrel{+}{\to} \mathbf{B}^2 A
          %h3#on_short_exact_sequences On short exact sequences
          %p
            In any category with products, for any object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal"} diagonal
            morphism
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi C
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo ×
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_C:C\to C\times C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∇
                    %mi C
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla_C: C\coprod C\to C
            (addition in the case of modules). Every additive category is, in particular, a category with finite
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/biproduct"} biproduct
            = succeed "-modules," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \to A_i \to \hat H_{i} \to G_i \to 0
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i = 1,2
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\to A_1\oplus A_2 \to H_1\oplus H_2\to G_1\oplus G_2\to 0
          %p
            Now if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi N
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\to M\to N\to P\to 0
            is any extension, call it
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma:P_1\to P
            a morphism, then there is a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ′
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mi M
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi β
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma' = (id_M,\beta_1,\gamma)
            from an extension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_1
            of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\to M\to N_1\to P_1\to 0
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E_1,\Gamma_1)
            is unique up to isomorphism of extensions, and it is called
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\gamma
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi P
                            %mn 1
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %msub
                            %mi β
                            %mn 1
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mi γ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi N
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  N_1&amp;\to &amp;P_1\\
                  \\downarrow\beta_1 &amp;&amp; \downarrow\gamma\\
                  N&amp;\to &amp;P
                  }
          %p
            is a pullback diagram. Every morphism of abelian extensions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi α
                  %mo ,
                  %mi β
                  %mo ,
                  %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\alpha,\beta,\gamma):E\to E'
            in a unique way decomposes as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi α
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi β
                        %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi id
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi E
                  %mi γ
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi id
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi β
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi E
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E\stackrel{(\alpha,\beta_a,id)}\longrightarrow E\gamma \stackrel{(id,\beta_ 1,\gamma)}\longrightarrow E'
          %p
            for some
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi β
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta_a
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi β
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta_1
            as above. In short, the morphism of extensions factorizes through
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\gamma
          %p
            Dually, for any morphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo :
                    %mi M
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha:M\to M_2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi α
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi β
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_2 = (\alpha,\beta_2,id_P)
            to an extension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_2
            of the form
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\to M_2\to N_2\to P
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E_2,\Gamma_2)
            is unique up to isomorphism of extensions and it is called
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha E
          %p In fact, the diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi M
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi N
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mi α
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %msub
                            %mi β
                            %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi M
                            %mn 2
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  M&amp;\to &amp;N\\
                  \\downarrow\alpha &amp;&amp; \downarrow\beta_2\\
                  M_2&amp;\to &amp;N_2
                  }
          %p
            is a pushout diagram. Every morphism of abelian extensions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi α
                  %mo ,
                  %mi β
                  %mo ,
                  %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                  %mo ″
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\alpha,\beta,\gamma):E\to E''
            in a unique way decomposes as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi α
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi β
                        %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi id
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi α
                  %mi E
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi id
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi β
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi E
                  %mo ″
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E\stackrel{(\alpha,\beta_a,id)}\longrightarrow \alpha E \stackrel{(id,\beta_ 2,\gamma)}\longrightarrow E''
          %p
            for some
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi β
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta_a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi β
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta_2
            as above. In short, the morphism of extensions factorizes through
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha E
          %p
            There are the following isomorphisms of extensions:
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi γ
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mi γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\alpha E)\gamma\cong \alpha (E\gamma)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi M
                    %mi E
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_M E \cong E
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi P
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E id_P \cong P
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo ′
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi E
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi α
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\alpha'\alpha)E\cong\alpha' (\alpha E)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mi γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi γ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi γ
                    %mi γ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E\gamma)\gamma' \cong E(\gamma\gamma')
          %p
            The Baer’s sum of two extensions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_1,E_2
            of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\to M\to N_i\to P\to 0
            (i.e. with the same
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∇
                      %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_1+E_2 = \nabla_M (E_1\oplus E_2) \Delta_P
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ext
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ext(P,M)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ext
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ext:\mathcal{A}^{op}\times\mathcal{A}\to Ab
            is a biadditive (bi)functor. This is also related to the isomorphisms of extensions
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi α
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi α
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha (E_1+E_2)\cong \alpha E_1+\alpha E_2
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi E
                    %mo ≅
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 1
                    %mi E
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 2
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\alpha_1+\alpha_2) E \cong \alpha_1 E+ \alpha_2 E
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi γ
                    %mo ≅
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mi γ
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E_1+E_2)\gamma \cong E_1\gamma + E_2\gamma
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi E
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi E
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(\gamma_1+\gamma_2)\cong E\gamma_1 + E\gamma_2
          %p
            In different notation, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \to A \to \hat G_{i} \to G \to 0
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i = 1,2
            are two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequences"} short exact sequences
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
            %strong Baer sum
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\hat G_1 + \hat G_2
                  \\coloneqq
                  +_* \Delta^* \hat G_1 \times \hat G_2
          %p
            The first step forms the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            of the short exact sequence along the diagonal on
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mi A
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi G
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ⊕
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi G
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi G
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ⊕
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi G
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi G
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi Δ
                                %mi G
                        %mtd
                          %mi G
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  A \oplus A &amp;\to&amp; A \oplus A
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\Delta^* (\hat G_1 \oplus \hat G_2) &amp;\to&amp; \hat G_1 \oplus \hat G_2
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  G &amp;\stackrel{\Delta_G}{\to}&amp;  G\oplus G
                  }
          %p
            The second forms the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
            along the addition map on
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi G
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ⊕
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi G
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %mo *
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi G
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ⊕
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi G
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi G
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  A \oplus A &amp;\stackrel{+}{\to}&amp; A
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\Delta^* (\hat G_1 \oplus \hat G_2) &amp;\to&amp; +_* \Delta^*(\hat G_1 \oplus \hat G_2)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  G &amp;\to&amp;  G
                  }
